  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Turn one fisheye canopy photo into gap fraction, effective and true leaf area index, clumping indices and mean leaf tilt angle by setting a circular lens mask and binarization and gap-fraction settings, then running a four-step Import → Binarize → Gap Fraction → Canopy Attributes pipeline. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
